<p>In the latest turn, the United States said its forces attacked and seized the Iranian-flagged cargo ship M/V Touska in the Gulf of Oman on April 19 after it allegedly tried to pass a US naval blockade near the Strait of Hormuz. President Trump said the vessel ignored repeated warnings, and US Central Command and multiple outlets said a Navy destroyer disabled the ship before Marines boarded it. Iran called the operation piracy and a violation of the two-week ceasefire due to expire on Wednesday, and Iranian officials vowed a response. The seizure adds new strain to an already fragile US-Iran ceasefire and casts fresh doubt on planned talks meant to prevent a wider conflict. Several reports said Washington was preparing to send a high-level delegation, including Vice President JD Vance, to Islamabad for negotiations, but Iranian state media and other outlets said Tehran had no plans to take part after the ship seizure. The stakes remain high because Iran has again moved to close or restrict the Strait of Hormuz, a key global energy chokepoint, fueling shipping disruption and higher oil prices even as diplomacy remains possible.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/CkZWL780jE9G9lgDNToChVB2mwL6fRMRuvTFY9n01t5uN-zdIce60RtMsHMqH605SGZyATo-d8r5lb8SJ-QZAmTxHJgCp_AOimJBoVkhfGctg9hm_KPeM-GoAa_sQgZWA7G6ZdLXxypRharEPxYcfYNUCwUpDqBOtoWS85Z_N5t1u_8GsYkfR7XYP8CAQXXcqUnIuzLYgoy53WQHvSVUriTIX9pAVzOOX0N8s_KeKIaOanUQBDH4XMQja_oo-lrCnDE' alt='A view of Iranian-flagged cargo ship Touska as USS Spruance intercepts it in video released on April 19, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Legal debate: Maritime and military law experts told The New York Times that the expanded US blockade has historical precedent, but it also raises legal and practical questions about how far that enforcement can reach.</li><li>Six-hour standoff: CENTCOM said Touska&#x27;s crew ignored warnings for six hours before USS Spruance disabled the ship, suggesting the interception was a prolonged coercive operation rather than a sudden strike.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US administration: President Trump said the ship tried to breach the blockade, and the White House said it was still sending a senior delegation to Pakistan for negotiations despite the new confrontation. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/04/19/world/iran-us-war-trump-hormuz'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Iranian military command: Iran&#x27;s joint military command called the boarding an act of piracy and said the United States had violated the ceasefire, warning that Tehran would retaliate soon. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-navy-seizes-iranian-flagged-ship-near-strait-of-hormuz-tehran-vows-swift-response/article70882994.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Iranian state media / diplomatic line: Tehran said it had no plans to join the new Islamabad talks after the ship seizure, signaling that the military clash was also derailing the peace track. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/world-weighs-fate-mideast-ceasefire-after-us-seizes-iranian-cargo-ship'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/04/19/nx-s1-5790487/u-s-says-it-seized-an-iranian-cargo-ship-ceasefire-expires-soon'>U.S. says it seized an Iranian cargo ship, ceasefire expires soon</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/19/2026/us-seizes-iranian-ship-as-strait-is-closed'>US seizes Iranian ship as strait is closed</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/04/20/us-captures-iranian-cargo-ship-that-tried-to-evade-hormuz-blockade-as-new-round-of-talks-is-prepared'>US captures Iranian cargo ship that tried to evade Hormuz blockade as new round of talks is prepared</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/iran-cargo-ship-seized-pakistan-ceasefire-negotiations/33735754.html'>US Fires On, Seizes Iranian Ship, While Fate Of Cease-Fire, Peace Talks Uncertain</a> - rferl.org</l